join Gogo (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
update Gogo (Warm)
Gogo: You have her walk.
- Whose?
	Hope: Whose?
	Gogo: Your grandmother's. I'd know it anywhere. I watched it cross this village for sixty years.
	Gogo: I'm Thandiwe. Everyone calls me Gogo now. Even people who aren't owed the right to.
	- I remember you. A little.
		Hope: I remember you. A little.
		Gogo: A little is more than most get, at your age when you left.
	- I'm sorry — I don't remember much
		Hope: I'm sorry — I don't remember much.
		Gogo: You were small. It isn't a debt you owe me.
- You knew my grandmother?
	Hope: You knew my grandmother?
	Gogo: Knew her. Argued with her. Buried two husbands and outlasted her by only a season.
	Gogo: She'd have liked watching you try to fix that roof.
Gogo: You found the boxes, then.
- How did you know?
	Hope: How did you know?
	Gogo: Because she never once, in forty years, threw anything away that might be useful later.
	Gogo: Half this village has something of hers holding it together. She just never told anyone which half.
set {GameState.gogo_confirmed_grandmother_boxes} = true
Gogo: Come by when you have a moment that isn't a task. I have all the time you could want, and most days nobody asks for it.
[signal arg="hearts:gogo:2"]
set {GameState.quest_gogo_reunion} = "complete"
[signal arg="unlock:Gogo Thandiwe active as standing NPC; gogo_ambient states become available"]
